Description: SCINET reconstructs cell-type- and cell-state-specific
    interactomes at single-cell resolution. It transforms single-cell
    expression into gene activity scores, subsamples cells to stabilise those
    scores, and rescores the edges of a reference interactome so that each
    cell population receives its own weighted network. The resulting ensemble
    supports analysis of gene-interaction dynamics and of the cell-type
    specificity of disease-associated perturbations.
